+  "content.90300c33c2a3": "Curated telemetry values. Controller execution is a simplified saturation model.",
+  "content.0ee9ffcefb2f": "Model management (October 16): master, dev and staging still use selector 20 with Chestnut v27 and Qualcomm v23. Published Chestnut v28 and Qualcomm v25 require selector 21; publication does not establish availability on those branches. PRs #2015, #2044 and #1999 were closed without merging; they are not released fixes.",
+  "content.7ed583d2f6de": "Master, dev and staging still use selector 20, Chestnut v27 and Qualcomm v23. The published Chestnut v28 and Qualcomm v25 catalogs require selector 21. Check your branch before selecting a model. PRs #2015 and #2044 were closed without merging. Refresh while parked with no download in progress; Clear Cache removes downloaded models.",
+  "content.8991ba93f76f": "Master, dev and staging use selector 20 and Chestnut v27 / Qualcomm v23. New v28 / v25 catalogs require selector 21. PRs #2015 and #2044 are closed without merging, not pending adoption. Sources: https://github.com/sunnypilot/sunnypilot/pull/2015 and https://github.com/sunnypilot/sunnypilot/pull/2044.",
+  "content.473919f486c6": "The wiki documents 132 models. Device availability depends on hardware, selector version and installed branch.",
+  "content.6071b9423bba": "Browse 132 documented driving models. Published catalog entries are not necessarily available on your device or branch.",
+  "content.fc0681438b1b": "Legacy contextual switching between Chill and Experimental longitudinal modes. PR #2056 removed DEC from master on October 16, 2026; the inspected dev build also omits it, while staging still retains it.",
+  "content.120a019dd418": "Legacy mode switching; removed from current master and dev.",
+  "content.7f68f41a61cb": "Check your installed branch. DEC is absent from inspected master/dev and remains in inspected staging. This change does not establish removal from older tagged releases. The setup wizard no longer automatically recommends this branch-dependent setting.",
+  "content.3556c2fdb03d": "Legacy automatic switching between Chill and Experimental modes; unavailable on inspected current master/dev.",
+  "content.1429b85c93d3": "For legacy builds that still implement DEC; not a recommendation for current master/dev.",
+  "content.7a8b08692e2e": "Removed from master by PR #2056 on October 16. Inspected dev omits DEC; staging retains it. Check branch and release notes before using this legacy setting.",
+  "content.388d32485bf6": "Removal source: https://github.com/sunnypilot/sunnypilot/pull/2056. Preserve older-build context; do not infer identical behavior across branches.",
+  "content.6d043f46fdf6": "PR #1999 proposed changes for a misleading Posenet NaN-speed alert during compiled-model startup, but was closed without merging on October 16, 2026.",
+  "content.6e8d1bdbce27": "Do not treat PR #1999 as an available fix. Persistent alerts still require runtime diagnostics; clearing the model cache alone does not establish a repaired runtime.",
+  "content.716581c145c4": "Published artifact only. No dedicated model poll or vehicle-specific driving evidence was verified in this audit.",
+  "content.b4bccd2140c7": "The official Chestnut v28 manifest lists this model with selector 21 and generation 12. Inspected master/dev/staging use selector 20 and Chestnut v27, so publication does not establish availability on those branches. Hardware and runtime compatibility must be checked.",
+  "content.163fb8300cd6": "Research with a compatible selector-21 runtime; no vehicle-specific recommendation is established.",
+  "content.9e2e02a27687": "Dynamic Experimental Control — legacy mode switching; removed from current master/dev, retained in inspected staging.",
+  "content.052c83176bf9": "These are the \"big models\" — chestnut-class networks larger than anything in the WMI or OP lines, tied to comma's new GPU add-on, which began reaching owners in August 2026. They drop under the forum's big_model tag on a near-daily cadence during a run. The extra network size shows up first in lateral: taking in-town 90-degree turns wide instead of cutting them, and showing planted rather than floaty highway stability. Standout entries like Cinque Terre and Sad Model have significantly improved lateral stability and natural steering feel, while earlier BMRLNAP runs suffered from low-speed steering oscillations. Stop signs and traffic light stop lines remain an active area of tuning across the line. Runtime notes (October 2): PR #2035 proposes 1344×760 comma 3X frames before unified AMD transfer. PR #2023 proposes ChestnutPowerLimit (0 = stock; 40–100 W) via advanced sunnylink Device controls on comma four. Both remain open. Model management (October 16): master, dev and staging still use selector 20 with Chestnut v27 and Qualcomm v23. Published Chestnut v28 and Qualcomm v25 require selector 21; publication does not establish availability on those branches. PRs #2015, #2044 and #1999 were closed without merging; they are not released fixes.",
+  "content.c98ae1d47d6c": "Model management (October 25): inspected master, dev and staging use selector 21, Chestnut v28 and Qualcomm v25. Mountain Dew Model v3 is their default big model. These development snapshots do not establish availability in older tagged releases. PRs #2015, #2044 and #1999 remain closed without merging.",
+  "content.940def03d2a7": "Inspected master, dev and staging now use selector 21, Chestnut v28 and Qualcomm v25, with Mountain Dew Model v3 as the default big model. Older builds use different catalogs. Check hardware and branch compatibility; refresh while parked with no download running. Clear Cache removes downloaded models.",
+  "content.acb24bbbc07c": "Inspected master/dev/staging now consume selector-21 catalogs: Chestnut v28 and Qualcomm v25. Older selector-20 builds use different catalogs. Check your installed version before refreshing. Source: https://github.com/sunnypilot/sunnypilot/blob/861fd118a1fe4ffec2283208456032b3616da968/openpilot/sunnypilot/models/fetcher.py.",
+  "content.5ce6409c775b": "The wiki documents 134 models. Device availability depends on hardware, selector version and installed branch.",
+  "content.d49b775b36e4": "Browse 134 documented driving models. A published catalog entry does not establish support on every device or older branch.",
+  "content.2523a7f769bd": "The maintainer announcement requires comma four plus Chestnut and explicitly excludes comma 3X for now. Inspected master/dev/staging use selector 21 and Chestnut v28; Mountain Dew Model v3 is the default big model. Check your installed build and hardware.",
+  "content.61b629644d41": "A dedicated maintainer forum topic and poll are now available. The overall poll has zero ratings in this snapshot, so no performance conclusion is established.",
+  "content.6a170c189509": "Published in Chestnut v28 with selector 21 and generation 12; included in the inspected master/dev/staging catalog. No model-specific comma 3X compatibility was verified. Confirm hardware and runtime support before use.",
+  "content.a42d426331ad": "Official artifact verified. No dedicated model poll or vehicle-specific driving feedback was verified in this scan.",
+  "content.18aa1ccb8a20": "Mountain Dew Model v3 is the default big model on the inspected branches; that is not a performance endorsement. Its announcement requires comma four plus Chestnut and excludes comma 3X for now. Train Track and Flip Flop have no verified dedicated poll.",
+  "content.f03773b9dc12": "Cinque Terre Model v2 is the previous default big model; inspected master/dev/staging now default to Mountain Dew Model v3. The maintainer recommends that comma 3X users stay on V2 while newer big-model support is pending. Hardware and branch compatibility still apply.",
+  "content.8dab9ce8fc76": "These are the \"big models\" — chestnut-class networks larger than anything in the WMI or OP lines, tied to comma's new GPU add-on, which began reaching owners in August 2026. They drop under the forum's big_model tag on a near-daily cadence during a run. The extra network size shows up first in lateral: taking in-town 90-degree turns wide instead of cutting them, and showing planted rather than floaty highway stability. Standout entries like Cinque Terre and Sad Model have significantly improved lateral stability and natural steering feel, while earlier BMRLNAP runs suffered from low-speed steering oscillations. Stop signs and traffic light stop lines remain an active area of tuning across the line. Runtime notes (October 2): PR #2035 proposes 1344×760 comma 3X frames before unified AMD transfer. PR #2023 proposes ChestnutPowerLimit (0 = stock; 40–100 W) via advanced sunnylink Device controls on comma four. Both remain open. Model management (October 25): inspected master, dev and staging use selector 21, Chestnut v28 and Qualcomm v25. Mountain Dew Model v3 is their default big model. These development snapshots do not establish availability in older tagged releases. PRs #2015, #2044 and #1999 remain closed without merging."
 }
